H('418.d.1',3,"An architect's client asks her to skip a required sprinkler system to cut costs. The ethical course is to:","explain the code requirement and keep the system",["omit it quietly","hide it from inspectors","let the contractor decide"],"Life-safety codes protect occupants.")
H('418.d.1',4,"A building designer notices that his firm's published project photos show features the firm did not design. Ethics requires him to:","correct the credit",["stay silent","add more false photos","delete the real drawings"],"Honest representation of work is an ethical duty.")
H('418.d.2.A',3,"A firm designing a school library begins by writing a clear statement of what the library must do. That is the first stage of the:","design process",["tax cycle","election cycle","weather cycle"],"Design starts with defining the problem.")
H('418.d.2.A',4,"After a mock-up of a stair shows the rise is too steep, the team revises the plans and builds a second mock-up. This repetition is called:","iteration",["abandonment","delegation","inflation"],"Iteration refines the design.")
H('418.d.2.B',3,"A client wants a 20-story tower on a lot that zoning limits to four stories. This conflict is a limit on the project's:","scope",["mascot","slogan","parking color"],"Regulation limits what is possible.")
H('418.d.2.B',4,"Selecting a cheaper insulation that fails the energy code is an ethical problem because it risks occupant:","safety and compliance",["decor","parking","menu"],"Ethics weighs more than savings.")
H('418.d.2.C',3,"Neighbors of a proposed apartment building are stakeholders because the building will change their street's:","traffic and views",["tax forms","recipes","playlists"],"Stakeholders include those affected.")
H('418.d.2.C',4,"A fire marshal who reviews a hotel design is a stakeholder whose main concern is:","life safety",["interior color","lobby music","staff uniforms"],"Different stakeholders have different priorities.")
H('418.d.2.D',3,"A scale model of a roof is loaded until it deflects too far. The failure is helpful because it shows what to strengthen before:","full-size construction",["a vacation","a party","a sale"],"Test failure improves the design.")
H('418.d.2.D',4,"Studies of the Hyatt Regency walkway collapse led engineers to improve how they review:","connection details",["paint colors","carpet samples","furniture styles"],"Failure analysis changes practice.")
H('418.d.4.A',3,"The part of a building that transfers its weight to the ground is the:","foundation",["canopy","awning","chimney cap"],"Foundations support the structure.")
H('418.d.4.A',4,"Walls, floors, roof, and foundation are all fundamental parts of a:","building",["landscape plan","traffic signal","bridge cable"],"These are the basic building elements.")
H('418.d.4.B',3,"Repeating windows in a regular pattern along a facade is an example of the visual design element of:","rhythm",["gravity","friction","inertia"],"Repetition creates rhythm.")
H('418.d.4.B',4,"A building that places a tall entrance tower at one end of a long low wing uses the design principle of:","emphasis",["erosion","corrosion","depreciation"],"A focal point draws attention.")
H('418.d.4.C',3,"Early settlers built homes from local materials such as logs and sod, showing that building styles often reflect available:","resources",["trophies","lyrics","coupons"],"Location shapes construction.")
H('418.d.4.C',4,"The invention of the elevator and steel frames made it possible to build the first:","skyscrapers",["pyramids","aqueducts","castles"],"Technology changed building height.")
H('418.d.5.A',3,"Wood, masonry, steel, and concrete are common building:","materials",["moods","languages","hobbies"],"These are structural materials.")
H('418.d.5.A',4,"A material made of fired clay blocks laid with mortar is called:","brick masonry",["glass curtain","steel plate","vinyl siding"],"Brick is a masonry unit.")
H('418.d.5.B',3,"Asphalt shingles, clay tiles, and metal panels are all common types of:","roofing",["flooring","plumbing","wiring"],"Roofing keeps weather out.")
H('418.d.5.B',4,"A roofing material that is very long lasting and sheds snow easily is:","standing seam metal",["thatch","newspaper","cardboard"],"Metal roofs are durable.")
H('418.d.5.C',3,"Building a house by nailing studs into a frame and then covering it with sheathing is called:","wood framing",["tilt-wall","slip forming","post-tensioning"],"Light-frame wood is traditional in houses.")
H('418.d.5.C',4,"Tilt-wall construction forms large concrete wall panels flat on the ground and then:","lifts them upright with a crane",["floats them downstream","freezes them","paints them first"],"Panels are tilted into place.")
H('418.d.5.D',3,"Building sections in a factory and shipping them to the site is called prefabricated or:","modular construction",["hand digging","demolition","land clearing"],"Factory construction speeds work.")
H('418.d.5.D',4,"Modular construction can reduce weather delays because most of the work is done:","indoors in a factory",["on the roof","at night only","in the rain"],"Controlled conditions speed work.")
H('418.d.5.E',3,"Standard building methods include casting concrete, cutting lumber, and:","joining materials with fasteners",["painting the sky","freezing steel","growing bricks"],"Basic methods shape raw materials.")
H('418.d.5.E',4,"Pouring liquid concrete into a form so it hardens into the desired shape is called:","casting",["tearing","slicing","sanding"],"Casting makes shapes by pouring.")
H('418.d.5.F',3,"A building in a hurricane zone may use impact-resistant windows because resilient materials help it survive:","severe storms",["parties","holidays","commercials"],"Resilience reduces damage.")
H('418.d.5.F',4,"Resilient materials often cost more at first, but they can save money by reducing repair costs after a:","disaster",["birthday","concert","game"],"Life-cycle thinking supports resilience.")
H('418.d.5.G',3,"A designer who must meet a green building rating may choose materials with recycled content because the rating rewards:","sustainability",["decoration","popularity","height"],"Certifications influence material choices.")
H('418.d.5.G',4,"The local climate affects material selection because heavy rain, heat, and snow each:","wear materials differently",["change the zip code","raise the sun","hide the foundation"],"Climate drives durability needs.")
H('418.d.6.A',3,"A local building code exists mainly to protect public health and:","safety",["profit","fashion","parking"],"Codes protect people.")
H('418.d.6.A',4,"Requiring smoke alarms in every bedroom is a building code that protects occupants from:","fire",["noise","pollen","traffic"],"Codes address specific hazards.")
H('418.d.6.B',3,"Land use regulations divide a city into districts such as residential, commercial, and:","industrial",["musical","edible","fictional"],"Zoning separates uses.")
H('418.d.6.B',4,"A zoning ordinance allows a corner store in a commercial district but not in a district zoned strictly:","single-family residential",["industrial heavy","downtown mixed","retail"],"Allowable uses vary by district.")
H('418.d.6.C',3,"Zoning controls land use and development by setting limits on building height, setbacks, and:","density",["music","color of the sky","tenant names"],"Zoning shapes growth.")
H('418.d.6.C',4,"A required front setback of 25 feet means a building must be placed at least 25 feet from the:","front property line",["back door","power meter","neighbor's roof"],"Setbacks are measured from property lines.")
H('418.d.6.D',3,"Ramps, elevators, and wide doorways are standard features that make a building accessible to people with:","disabilities",["pets only","tools only","cameras"],"Accessibility features support all users.")
H('418.d.6.D',4,"An accessible parking space is located near the entrance so a person who uses a wheelchair can travel a shorter:","distance",["color","mood","tax"],"Closer spaces reduce travel.")
H('418.d.6.E',3,"Fire codes limit how far a person must travel to reach an exit, which constrains a building's:","floor plan layout",["paint colors","mascot","insurance form"],"Egress rules shape plans.")
H('418.d.6.E',4,"A code that limits the height of a combustible building to a few stories constrains a designer's choice of:","construction type",["wallpaper","carpet color","phone system"],"Codes limit what types may be used.")
H('418.d.6.F',3,"Energy codes require minimum insulation, which constrains the design of a building's:","walls and roof",["parking stripes","fonts","menu"],"Energy rules shape envelope design.")
H('418.d.6.F',4,"A building envelope that fails the energy code can be sent back for redesign before the owner receives a:","certificate of occupancy",["holiday card","gift","trophy"],"Code review precedes occupancy.")
H('418.d.6.G',3,"A building used for sleeping, such as an apartment, is classified by its occupancy as:","residential",["storage","assembly","industrial"],"Occupancy describes use.")
H('418.d.6.G',4,"A building's use type, occupancy, and construction type together determine which code requirements apply, such as the number of required:","exits",["colors","windows only","trees"],"Classification drives rules.")
H('418.d.7.A',3,"Tilt-wall panels, glass curtain walls, and brick veneer are different types of building:","envelopes",["foundations","elevators","signs"],"The envelope is the exterior shell.")
H('418.d.7.A',4,"The building envelope separates the conditioned interior from the exterior, so it controls heat, air, and:","moisture",["music","traffic","tenants"],"The envelope is a barrier.")
H('418.d.7.B',3,"The foundation, walls, windows, and roof are all components of the building:","envelope",["elevator","directory","signage"],"These form the shell.")
H('418.d.7.B',4,"A roof that leaks in a heavy rain has failed in its role as part of the building's:","water barrier",["stair system","fire alarm","parking plan"],"The roof sheds water.")
H('418.d.7.C',3,"Fiberglass batts, spray foam, and rigid board are all types of:","insulation",["lighting","paint","flooring"],"Insulation slows heat flow.")
H('418.d.7.C',4,"Insulation is rated by R-value, and a higher R-value means the material is better at resisting:","heat flow",["noise only","color change","moisture only"],"R-value measures thermal resistance.")
H('418.d.7.D',3,"Double-hung, casement, and sliding styles describe different types of building:","windows",["roofs","slabs","footings"],"Window types differ in operation.")
H('418.d.7.D',4,"Low-E coatings on glass help reduce heat transfer, so they are used on energy-efficient:","windows",["driveways","floors","chimneys"],"Coatings reduce heat flow.")
H('418.d.7.E',3,"The heating, ventilation, and air conditioning system, or HVAC, controls a building's indoor:","temperature and air quality",["street names","property taxes","wall colors"],"HVAC conditions air.")
H('418.d.7.E',4,"Ductwork in an HVAC system carries conditioned air from the equipment to the:","rooms",["foundation","attic fire","street"],"Ducts deliver air.")
H('418.d.7.F',3,"A building that earns a LEED rating has been recognized for meeting standards of green:","performance",["height","size","age"],"LEED rates sustainability.")
H('418.d.7.F',4,"Pursuing a LEED certification can influence the choice of mechanical equipment because efficient systems earn:","rating credits",["fines","complaints","delays"],"Credits reward efficiency.")
H('418.d.7.G',3,"An electrical system brings power from the utility through a service panel and then through branch circuits to outlets and:","lights",["pipes","ducts","windows"],"Circuits deliver power.")
H('418.d.7.G',4,"A circuit breaker in the panel protects a circuit from overload by:","shutting off the current",["adding more current","lowering the voltage","painting the wire"],"Breakers trip to prevent overheating.")
